  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 335 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nQuieter conditions are expected as we head into Sunday, with upper \nridging expected to amplify across the central CONUS as we head into \nearly next week. In fact, the upper pattern begins to transition \ntowards an omega block pattern, with the central US positioned \nbetween a cutoff low just off the coast of the eastern US and a deep \nupper low over the southwestern US. This leaves the area under the \ninfluence of the aforementioned upper ridging through the middle of \nnext week, and lead to high temperatures moderating back into the \n70s for all by Tuesday (70s expected Sat/Sun across western NE). \nLocations across southwest Nebraska will make a run at the lower 80s \nby midweek. This will also coincide with drier conditions, though \nfire concerns look to remain low due to surface dewpoints increasing \nback into the lower 50s. This will keep minimum afternoon humidity \nelevated in the 30-40% range, along with winds generally remaining \nbelow 20 miles per hour each day. In all, this points to a return of \npleasant fall weather, with mostly sunny, dry, and mild conditions \nreturning through the middle of next week.\n\nBy late week, the western US upper low will begin to eject east \nacross the Rockies by late Friday, bringing a return of \nsouthwesterly flow aloft. At the surface, low pressure will begin to \neject across the Dakotas by Friday evening, and this drags a cold \nfront into the area sometime Saturday. This looks to bring a return \nof cooler highs and some threat for precipitation as we head into \nnext weekend, and this will need to be monitored going forward.",
